# ============================================================
# DEPRECATED / LEGACY CONTENT — KEPT ON PURPOSE (v8.4.0 decision)
# ============================================================
# These directories are kept visible (not ignored) to document the project's
# evolution from v7 → v8.4.0. Future contributors and AI agents should SEE the
# legacy code to understand what was removed, why, and what replaced it.
#
# Each `_deprecated/` subdirectory has its own README.md explaining its content.
# Use `git log --follow <file>` to trace moves and decisions across versions.
#
# Decision rationale (2026-06-23, user-mandated):
#   "laisse les deprecated pour qu'ils comprennent que je reviens de loin"
#   — leaving the journey visible is part of the project's narrative.
# ============================================================
# DO NOT add `_deprecated/` to this file. If you want to ignore a NEW
# _deprecated subdir, add a specific exception to this comment block.

# Runtime logs (daemon stdout/stderr, watchdog, MCP server)
*.log
logs/
mathir_mcp/logs/
daemon_*.log
daemon_*.txt

# Claude Code local settings (contains machine-specific hook paths)
.claude/

# MiMoCode local state (plans, node_modules)
.mimocode/

# Codex local settings (contains machine-specific python paths + hook commands).
# Use mathir_mcp/codex_templates/ for the shareable templates instead.
.codex/
/hooks.json

# OpenCode plugin / config (machine-specific)
# (already covered via .claude/ pattern elsewhere if needed)

# Superpowers (agent scratch dirs)
.superpowers/
superpowers/

# Windows PowerShell `> nul` artifact (reserved device name)
nul
NUL

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment / secrets — NEVER commit keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env.local
*.env.production
*.env.development

# Private files — outreach templates (not for public repo)
docs/OUTREACH.md

# Downloaded benchmark datasets (large / re-downloadable via download_datasets.py)
benchmarks/05_test_data/longmemeval/
benchmarks/05_test_data/locomo/

# Source textbook PDFs used to build the fluid_mechanics BEIR benchmark
# dataset -- large (~28.5MB / ~23.8MB) and likely copyrighted, never for
# redistribution. The derived corpus.jsonl/queries.jsonl/qrels ARE committed
# (see benchmarks/05_test_data/beir_data/fluid_mechanics/), only the raw
# source PDFs are excluded.
benchmarks/Fluid_mecanique_book/*.pdf
